From: Linux agent, Surface Pro 11 IMX681 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] libcamera: add a camera_sensor_properties entry for IMX681

Without an entry libcamera logs

    WARN CameraSensor 'imx681 1-0010': No static properties available for 'imx681'

and falls back to a default unit cell, which makes every physical-size
property (field of view, focal length in 35 mm equivalent) wrong.

The unit cell size comes from the Windows camera profile
IMX681DeLoB35P3A5.json, recovered from the Surface Pro 11 driver store by the
Windows side of this relay. It gives pixel_width_mm and pixel_height_mm both as
0.001, i.e. 1000 nm square -- so the square assumption is measured, not inferred
from the array aspect ratio.

sensorDelays is left zeroed on purpose. libcamera treats an all-zero delay
block exactly like a missing entry (camera_sensor_legacy.cpp:498), so the
unverified defaults still apply and the "No sensor delays found" warning still
prints. That is the honest state: we have the cell size and we do not have the
delays, and inventing plausible numbers to silence a warning is how you get a
subtly wrong AE loop that nobody looks at again.

Verified after installing:

    Property: UnitCellSize = 1000x1000
    Property: PixelArraySize = 4032x3024
    Property: PixelArrayActiveAreas = [ (8, 64)/4032x3024 ]

Applies to the Ubuntu libcamera 0.7.0-1ubuntu2 source package, on top of
0001-ipa-libipa-add-CameraSensorHelper-for-IMX681.patch. The context differs
slightly from upstream v0.7.0 because the distro adds its own imx500 entry
just above.

--- a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
@@ -309,6 +309,23 @@
 				.hblankDelay = 3
 			},
 		} },
+		{ "imx681", {
+			/*
+			 * Unit cell size from the Windows camera profile
+			 * IMX681DeLoB35P3A5.json, which gives pixel_width_mm and
+			 * pixel_height_mm as 0.001 -- 1000 nm square. Measured
+			 * rather than inferred from the aspect ratio.
+			 *
+			 * sensorDelays is deliberately left zeroed. The delays
+			 * are unknown for this part, and an all-zero entry keeps
+			 * libcamera's unverified defaults *and* its warning,
+			 * which is the honest state. Guessing them here would
+			 * silence the warning without earning it.
+			 */
+			.unitCellSize = { 1000, 1000 },
+			.testPatternModes = {},
+			.sensorDelays = { },
+		} },
 		{ "imx708", {
 			.unitCellSize = { 1400, 1400 },
 			.testPatternModes = {
